  "note": "An intermediate voice week at 22 minutes a day, built from every singing tool so no two days look alike: leaps are the key skill and return daily in new forms (heard in the ear game, sung from Do in interval-singer with and without the picture, inside melody-singer tunes in two keys by a choice Key selector, and in lines over a backing-track), with breathwork to open, runs from run-singer, sight-singing, and a harmony line that comes back faster in choice stages.",
  "plan": {
    "title": "Week 1: leaps, runs and a line of your own",
    "summary": "Sing 4ths, 5ths and octaves in tune, first from Do, then inside tunes and over chords. Each day opens with breath, has an ear game or a run in the middle, and ends with a tune in two keys and a line you make up.",
    "progress": "Breath & range: in, hold and out from 4 counts up to 10, a hiss into a buzz, a long even breath out. Next: counts up to 12, and holding the high Do.\nPitch: slides and then leaps cleanly from Do to the high Do over an A drone. Next: the same without the slide first.\nIntervals & leaps: hears 3rds, 4ths, 5ths, 6ths and octaves rising, falling and together, sings the 3rd, 4th, 5th and octave up from Do in six keys from C to A, also without seeing the voice. Falling leaps are sung only inside tunes so far. Next: sing them down from Do, and sing the 6th.\nRuns: five-note run in eighths and sixteenths, a run with turns, a nine-note run, each up by semitones. Next: the octave run, slowly.\nMelodies: medium tunes with a 4th, a 5th and an octave in D and F, four short tunes read from the staff before hearing them. Next: longer tunes to read.\nHarmony & improvising: holds roots and a Mi Fa Re Mi line over I-IV-V-I in D and F up to 90, makes up lines from Do Mi Sol over four chords. Next: a line a 3rd above a tune.",
